From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: report charging while HL7139 direct charge is active

During direct charging the HL7139 charge pumps feed the battery
directly and the Qualcomm PMIC buck is quiesced to 13 mA. The
battery-manager firmware only tracks its own charger, so it reports
the battery as Discharging even while the pumps push ~4.8 A into the
cell. UPower/SteamOS then shows the wrong icon.

When the firmware reports the battery is not charging via the PMIC
path, consult the HL7139 pump supplies: if either is online, report
the battery as Charging. On devices without the pumps the lookup
finds nothing and behavior is unchanged.

Signed-off-by: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -533,6 +533,37 @@
 
 	switch (psp) {
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_STATUS:
+		/*
+		 * During direct charging the HL7139 charge pumps feed the
+		 * battery and the Qualcomm buck is quiesced to 13 mA. The
+		 * battery-manager firmware only tracks its own buck, so it
+		 * reports DISCHARGING even while the pumps push current into
+		 * the cell. If either pump supply is online, the battery is
+		 * charging by definition.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->status.status != POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING) {
+			static const char * const pump_names[] = {
+				"hl7139-master", "hl7139-slave",
+			};
+			struct power_supply *pump;
+			union power_supply_propval pval;
+			int i;
+
+			for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(pump_names); i++) {
+				pump = power_supply_get_by_name(pump_names[i]);
+				if (!pump)
+					continue;
+				if (!power_supply_get_property(pump,
+							      POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_ONLINE,
+							      &pval) &&
+				    pval.intval) {
+					power_supply_put(pump);
+					val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
+					return 0;
+				}
+				power_supply_put(pump);
+			}
+		}
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.status;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_TYPE:
